76 to 1503.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/pierre-de-breze"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pierre-de-breze.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Pierre de Brézé</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Pierre de Brézé was a French nobleman, soldier and leading adviser of Charles VII, grand seneschal of Normandy.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/pierre-de-castelnau"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pierre-de-castelnau.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Pierre de Castelnau</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Pierre de Castelnau was a Cistercian monk and papal legate sent by Pope Innocent III to combat Catharism in Languedoc.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/pierre-de-la-baume"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pierre-de-la-baume.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Pierre de La Baume</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Pierre de La Baume was bishop of Geneva from 1522 and the last bishop to reside in the city.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/pierre-de-rigaud-marquis-de-vaudreuil-cavagnial"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pierre-de-rigaud-marquis-de-vaudreuil-cavagnial.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Pierre de Rigaud, Marquis de Vaudreuil-Cavagnial</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Pierre de Rigaud, Marquis de Vaudreuil-Cavagnial, was the last governor general of New France, from 1755 to 1760, and the first born in Canada.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/pierre-deval"><span class="enc-name">Pierre Deval</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class